{"kind":"event","event_id":9113,"event_uid":"01M2Q4994F1NQN3ATK43874MRW","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":383,"issue_uid":"01M2Q44J0XTFMSVZW0XH87A4D3","issue_short_id":"a4d3","actor":"impl:3@run-178","hlc_physical_ms":1789630129295,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"55d99f49a80f12d5608862fd5b1fac9f39c2c64ce854360efd95ecc9ad82d0c0","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2Q4994E9BD4BDJTM22DT3QQ","author":"impl:3@run-178","body":"Task 3 approach: three doc edits, no code. (1) CONTRACT.md evidence listing — extend the `residuals.jsonl` sentence with the `jev` object (kind.status/kind.subject/actor/attention/claim_false/confidence/model, absent-not-null on failure) and add a `residuals-jev.jsonl` sentence in the same shape inside the same window, before `kata.jsonl`. (2) Publish bullet — insert the `Act on these: <q> of <n>` clause as one more `then …;` member between the mutant/table sentence and the `Residuals: <n> from review` clause (so test_sandbox_boot_card_cells leg (c) keeps its range), and add the '— the errands and the `Act on these` rows excepted' phrase to the reviewer's-sentence line. (3) RUNBOOK.md Traps — new `**TypeSafe.**` label with exactly two rows between **The Claude proxy.** and **The GitHub edge.**, taking the Traps row count 40 -> 42. Wrapping matters: every phrase a Run: leg pins must sit unbroken on one line, since the folds are `tr '\\n' ' '` and leave the continuation indent as extra spaces.","created_at":"2026-09-17T07:28:49.294423404Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-17T07:28:49.295Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":9116,"event_uid":"01M2Q4A66VF5EWDW7D3S115JXY","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":382,"issue_uid":"01M2Q44E8XJJKR1ZG0J6KC1BEQ","issue_short_id":"1beq","actor":"impl:1@run-178","hlc_physical_ms":1789630159067,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"a75d8a223cd1b3e72a50bb66f06fd115e4a9194649aecf6f836c009ced68f301","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2Q4A66TXDSZ0G3SPBKN0A6E","author":"impl:1@run-178","body":"Approach for task 1 (the boot asks Jev about every residual row):\n\n- `TYPESAFE_URL=\"${FLEET_TYPESAFE_URL:-https://typesafe.int.exe.xyz}\"` beside `KATA_URL` (line ~127); `RESIDUALS_JEV_FILE=\"residuals-jev.jsonl\"` beside `RESIDUALS_FILE` (line ~148).\n- `residual_read` stays the ONE reader and grows a third mode. Its argv gains the plan path and the cache path. Mode `jev` emits one tab-separated `<key>\\t<name>\\t<payload>` line per item whose sha256 key the cache does not already carry; mode `rows` merges a cached reply's answers into the row as `jev`.\n- A new `residual_jev` bash function loops over that reader output (written to a temp file, so the loop body is not in a pipeline subshell), makes one `fleet_curl -fsS --max-time 10 -X POST -H 'content-type: application/json' -d \"$body\" \"$TYPESAFE_URL/v1/systemone\"` per line, appends one cache line, and logs `jev: <name> — curl exit <n>` on a non-zero exit. Called from `collect_evidence` just before the ledger write, so the cache is what makes it one request per item per run across every transition.\n- Rig: one `*typesafe.int.exe.xyz/v1/systemone)` arm in `STUBS.curl` before the `*)` fallthrough, with `STUB_TYPESAFE_EXIT`, `STUB_TYPESAFE_ANSWERS` (needle TAB reply) and `STUB_TYPESAFE_ANSWER` knobs, payload appended to $FLEET_HOME/typesafe.log.","created_at":"2026-09-17T07:29:19.066503473Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-17T07:29:19.067Z"}
